.Dd $Mdocdate: September 22 2026 $
.Dt FUGUPASS-QR 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm fugupass-qr
.Nd FuguPass QR render helper
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads the standard input, and it writes one QR code to the standard
output.
.Xr fugupass 1
runs it as a child, and it takes no option and no argument.
.Pp
The code reaches the terminal as UTF-8 half blocks.
One character carries two module rows.
A block half is a light module, and a space half is a dark module.
Each code carries a quiet zone of 4 light modules on each side.
.Pp
The bytes of the input give the shape of the code.
An input of 12 words of the BIP39 English list is a mnemonic, with
one space between two words and at most one line feed at the end.
.Nm
renders such an input as a Standard SeedQR: version 2, level L,
numeric mode, and mask pattern 0.
The payload is the zero-based index of each word, in four decimal
digits.
A signer scans that one form from the screen.
.Pp
Every other input is a vault file, and
.Nm
renders it at level L in byte mode, at the lowest version that takes
the file.
The one-code capacity is 2953 bytes.
.Nm
reports a longer file, and it writes no code.
A vault file is ciphertext, so the paper copy of such a code is a
safe backup.
.Pp
.Nm
holds
.Dv RLIMIT_CORE
at zero, before every other act of the program.
It reads the limit with
.Xr getrlimit 2 ,
and it calls
.Xr setrlimit 2
only when the limit is not zero.
.Xr fugupass 1
holds the limit at zero, and a child of it inherits that limit.
The execpromises of that process hold no
.Dq proc
promise, so a
.Xr setrlimit 2
call of such a child is a pledge violation.
A crash of
.Nm
writes no core file.
.Pp
.Nm
then pledges
.Dq stdio .
It opens no file, it creates no process, and it reaches no network.
.Pp
The words of a mnemonic are the master of the vault, so the input of
.Nm
can be a secret.
The program clears each buffer of its own before it exits.
.Sh THE ENCODER
.Nm
encodes each code with
.Sy libqrencode ,
by Kentaro Fukuchi.
FuguPass holds no source of that library, and the port of FuguPass
declares the package of it as a library dependency.
.Nm
links the shared library, and it runs no program of that package.
.Pa docs/analysis/qr-library-sources.md
of the FuguPass source tree records the evaluation of each QR
library: the provenance of it, the license of it, and the cost of
it.
.Pp
The library picks the mask pattern of a code by penalty score, and a
mnemonic code must carry pattern 0.
.Nm
therefore re-masks such a code.
.Pp
The library frees the digit buffer of an input with
.Xr free 3 ,
and it erases no byte of that buffer.
The digits of a mnemonic therefore stay in the freed heap of this
process, and
.Nm
cannot reach that memory.
The program renders one code, and it then exits.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
The
.Nm
utility exits 0 after it writes one code.
It exits 1 on each failure below.
.Bl -bullet
.It
The sandbox call of the program fails.
.It
The command line holds an argument.
.It
The read of the standard input fails.
.It
The input holds no byte.
.It
The input is longer than the one-code capacity.
.It
The encode of the input fails.
.It
The code of a mnemonic carries another version than 2.
.It
The write of the code fails.
.El
.Pp
Every report goes to the standard error.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr fugupass 1 ,
.Xr fugupass-scan 1 ,
.Xr getrlimit 2 ,
.Xr pledge 2
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Dick Olsson Aq Mt hi@senzilla.io
